# quality-gate — free-text polish via quality-loop (qloop) on mini (Tier L)

## When to use

Use this skill for **multi-constraint free-text** answers with **no tool/test
oracle**: risk lists, rollback plans, proposals, ops runbooks, careful Q&A.

**Do not use** for:
- Code edits / diffs (OpenCode + tests own that path)
- Client-confidential work over Telegram/Discord (use dashboard/SSH only)
- Tasks tagged `GATE: skip` or pure plumbing ("restart service X")

## How to run

Shell out (PATH includes `/usr/local/bin` after agentlab provision):

```bash
{{ hermes_quality_gate_script }} \
  --task "…" \
  [--baseline "existing draft"] \
  --strategy refine \
  --worker general \
  [--playbook /data/agentlab/playbooks/writing.md|/data/agentlab/playbooks/infra.md]
```

Stdout is one JSON object. Honor it:

| decision | exit | action |
|----------|------|--------|
| ACCEPT or KEEP_BASELINE | 0 | return `answer` to the user |
| SKIP | 2 | return original draft / answer without looping |
| FAIL | 1 | surface `reason`; do not invent content |

Defaults: strategy=refine, worker=general, judge=general, rounds=2, timeout=180s.
Only warm models (`general`, `coder`) are allowed — never `heavy`/`judge`/`scout`.

## Playbooks

- `/data/agentlab/playbooks/writing.md` — client-facing prose
- `/data/agentlab/playbooks/infra.md` — lab/ops free-text

Do **not** run playbook reflect from chat. Reflect only after a known PASS/FAIL
outcome via `qloop playbook reflect` or suite `--reflect`.

## Tier

Always Tier L: inference on mini (`{{ hermes_ollama_base_url }}`). Never send
client-confidential material to xAI/Grok through this path.
